{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1016","id":4946629425,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJgfwyc8AAAABJteTMQ","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1016","diff_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1016.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1016.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1016","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1016/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1016/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1016/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/statuses/5f3ecdf93e762a1b1551b44977a44f2e63c97802","number":1016,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(channel): preserve recovery readiness after migrated cluster restart","user":{"login":"tangtaoit","id":3895878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU4Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3895878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit","html_url":"https://github.com/tangtaoit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary / 变更摘要\n\nAfter original-v2 migration and a cluster restart, incomplete recovery proof could escape as a generic HTTP 400 and stop history reads. Preserve public `ErrNotReady` identity for the two transient proof states so reads return the existing retryable 503 contract; retain permanent error causes, quorum proof and write fencing.\n\nKeep the complete-history migration assertions aligned with acknowledged business sequences when recovery barriers consume log positions. Fix cross-node authentication fixtures, add authenticated self-chat/restart coverage, and add credential-free Linux default-suite plus migration/messaging E2E acceptance. The candidate runner records original outcomes and reclaims only its owned session, including independently grouped product nodes.\n\nThis is the small integration PR selected from `codex/v3-rc-qualification`; its product and dependency trees match qualified candidate `ef798352c40a94e57f768f76b2f4713712f827fe`. The [complete evidence branch](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/tree/138737b94/docs/reports) preserves initial failures and attribution limitations without exceeding the Review Agent's 50-file limit in this PR. No release tag, cloud purchase, production channel enablement, or protected Review/Issue Agent control change is included.\n\n## Release notes / 发布说明\n\n- [x] I added every user-visible change to `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]`.\n- [ ] This pull request has no user-visible change. I explained why below and a maintainer added the `skip-changelog` label.\n\n## Verification / 验证\n\n- Migration repair: five topologies passed, 55 complete-history observations, plus cold/hot and Channel failover regressions. [Frozen report](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/blob/32d402f7625c36f5667a290ec95c045f5f35937c/docs/reports/2026-10-20-v3-migration-recovery-repair.md).\n- Qualified product candidate: unchanged Linux conversation floor 20/20, 43,800 completed requests, zero errors/drops, max P99 75.80928 ms; [run 39453556254](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/actions/runs/39453556254).\n- Local default-package coverage: 219 passed, 15 no-test packages. Initial disk/cache build failures are retained; only the 102 cache-failed packages were rebuilt with a dedicated cache. This is aggregate coverage, not a claim that the first full command passed.\n- New self-chat: both single-node and three-node clusters passed; 12 ACKs, 12 complete-history checks, two whole-cluster restarts. Initial pagination/Close fixture failures are retained; no product change was made for them.\n- `flow-doc-contracts`, `workflow-contracts`, seven workflow static contracts, actionlint and shell syntax checks passed. Real-process runner probes cover independent PGID cleanup, success, exit 7, timeout, output limit, SIGTERM and unreadable inventory; Linux `/proc` is to be exercised by this PR's CI.\n- Candidate Linux, SDK, Manager, native-package and three-node CI: pending this exact PR source; results will be recorded before declaring candidate integration qualified.\n\nThe CPU attribution experiment does not prove beta-to-candidate non-regression and is not a new release gate. Formal RC long-run stages and signed stable native-package publication remain separate pending work; this PR does not claim formal v3 readiness.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T04:58:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T04:58:32Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"0ab6ea4bad09c76dae8c71f8ca67c00d4e220b89","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"WuKongIM:codex/v3-release-recovery","ref":"codex/v3-release-recovery","repo":{"id":638054601,"node_id":"R_kgDOJgfwyQ","name":"WuKongIM","full_name":"WuKongIM/WuKongIM","owner":{"login":"WuKongIM","id":132860831,"node_id":"O_kgDOB-tLnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132860831?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM","followers_url":"https://api